    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to introduce 30 Oaklands Park, a superb Edwardian, red brick home in a highly sought after location to the open market. Set along one of Sandymount's most desirable residential streets, this exceptional five-bedroom terraced home combines period charm with contemporary comfort. Beautifully extended and presented in turnkey condition, the property offers generous, light-filled accommodation ideal for modern family living, all within walking distance of Sandymount Village, the seafront, and excellent junior and senior schools. \n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 200 sq mt and flows effortlessly, blending traditional proportions with a modern extension that enhances both space and natural light. Well-appointed reception rooms provide flexibility for family living, entertaining, or working from home, while the overall layout offers excellent separation between living and sleeping accommodation. The accommodation comprises: entrance hall, drawing room, living room, kitchen, dining/family room, guest WC and cloakroom (with built-in storage) and upstairs there are five generously proportioned bedrooms (two with ensuites and master with additional walk-in-wardrobe, one bathroom and utility room.\n\nTo the front, a small railed garden enhances the home's kerb appeal while providing privacy from the street. The landscaped rear garden is a true highlight—thoughtfully designed and low maintenance, it offers an inviting outdoor retreat perfect for dining al fresco, relaxing, or family play.\n\nOaklands Park is a quiet, mature residential road in the heart of Sandymount, prized for its sense of community and proximity to excellent amenities. Sandymount Village, the DART, Sandymount Strand, and a range of top schools are all within easy reach, while Dublin city centre and the IFSC are readily accessible. \n\nViewing of this fine family home comes highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 7.58m x 1.71m\nSpacious entrance hall with wooden floor, coving and understairs storage\n\nDrawing Room - 4.04m x 3.71m\nBeautiful reception room overlooking the front garden with cast iron fireplace and open fire, coving, centre rose, carpet and opening to…\n\nLiving Room - 3.98m x 3.27m\nReception room with coving, centre rose, carpet, door to inner courtyard and door to kitchen\n\nKitchen - 6.09m x 2.97m\nWonderful, fully fitted Bulthaup kitchen with ample eye and base level units, integrated induction hob, integrated undercounter freezer, integrated full size fridge, integrated dishwasher, integrated double oven and warming drawer, pull out bins, poured terrazzo floor (with underfloor heating) and opening to...\n\nDining/ Family Room - 8.95m x 4.41m\nLarge open plan, light filled room overlooking the rear garden with ample Velux windows, poured Terrazzo floor 9wih underfloor heating) feature painted brick wall, window seat and built-in desk area and alcove built to accommodate an upright piano\n\nGuest WC - 2.94m x 1m\nWith WC, Belfast sink, wall tiles and polished concrete floor\n\nCloakroom - \nCoat hanging area with two deep drawers, four built-in lockers, poured Terrazzo floor with underfloor heating\n\nLanding - 7.03m x 1.70m\nWith carpet and doors leading to…\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.13m x 2.93m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear garden with carpet, built-in desk, shelving and wardrobes\n\nUtility Room - 2.13m x 1.95m\nWith built-in units, Belfast sink and plumbed for washing machine\n\nBedroom 1 - 5.62m x 3.22m\nLarge master bedroom overlooking the front of the property with carpet and opening to…\n\nWalk-in wardrobe - 2.79m x 1.39m\nBuilt-in wardrobes with a selection of hanging space, shelving and drawers\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.39m x 1.75m\nWith WC, WHB with pink marble vanity, step-in power shower, floor tiles, part tiled walls and built-in swivel mirror\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.39m x 1.83m\nSingle bedroom overlooking the front of the property with built-in shelving, storage and desk area and carpet\n\nLanding - 5.97m x 1.72m\nWith carpet\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.44m x 2.98m\nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear of the property with built-in wardrobes, drawers and carpet\n\nBathroom - 2.72m x 2.09m\nWith WC, WHB with vanity unit, bath with shower over, floor tiles, part tiled walls and heated towel rail\n\nLanding - 2.75m x 1.85m\nWith carpet and large storage area behind built-in bookshleves\n\nBedroom 5 - 6.56m x 3.60m\nDual aspect double bedroom on the top floor with dormer window, built-in wardrobes and shelving unit\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.63m x 1.01m\nWith WC, WHB, heated towel rail, step-in power shower and floor tiles\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Superb Edwardian family home</li><li> Charming and characterful interiors</li><li> Extended and modernised recently</li><li> Residents on street parking</li><li> Landscaped rear garden with rear pedestrian access and garden shed</li><li> Sash windows</li><li> Five generously proportioned bedrooms</li><li> Excellent location equidistant to Ballsbridge and Sandymount</li><li> Close to a choice of sought after junior and senior schools and many sports clubs in the area.</ul>"
